.TH scan_eolskip 3
.SH NAME
scan_eolskip \- skip line terminator sequences
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <lib/scan.h>

size_t \fBscan_eolskip\fR(const char *\fIs\fR, size_t \fIlimit\fR);
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBscan_eolskip\fR checks if the string \fIs\fR begins with a line terminator.
It recognizes both CR+LF ("\er\en") and LF ("\en") sequences.
It will not look beyond \fIlimit\fR bytes.

.SH RETURN VALUE
\fBscan_eolskip\fR returns the number of bytes consumed (1 for "\en", 2 for "\er\en")
if a terminator is found. Returns 0 if no terminator is found at the start of \fIs\fR.